# Python bytecode caches.
#
# These are build artifacts, but they are also a leak vector this repo has already
# been bitten by: CPython stamps the ABSOLUTE source path of every compiled module
# into the .pyc, so a committed __pycache__ publishes the author's home directory.
# This repo is public.
#
# The leak scanner cannot defend this by itself: `leak-scan.sh --staged` reads the
# staged *text* diff, and a binary file produces no `+` lines, so it scans an empty
# string and passes. Its tree mode skips binaries outright (`grep -Iq .`). Ignoring
# the files is therefore the only layer that actually holds.
#
# The one .pyc that was already tracked despite this rule — git keeps tracking a file
# once it is in the index — was untracked on 2026-08-09 with:
#   git rm --cached wms2/specs/_verify/prehandoff/__pycache__/qa-view-orders.cpython-313.pyc
# Working tree at the time of removal contained the absolute path
# /Users/<author>/.../prehandoff/qa-view-orders.py, so the removal is a leak fix, not tidying.
# STILL OPEN: that path is in already-published history and untracking does not rewrite it.
# Purging it needs the history rewrite that is pending owner approval — a separate decision.
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo

# Runner output written by `qa-<screen>.py --json <name>`.
#
# The eight prehandoff runners write wherever `--json` points, so a verification pass
# that runs the suite leaves result files in the tree. They are a re-runnable measurement,
# not a record: the record is the `m1-`/`m2-`/`rv-` reports next to them. Ignoring them
# keeps `git add -A` from turning one pass's local run into a committed artefact.
#
# NOT ignored, deliberately, and do not add them here: the four *cited* snapshots
# `_verify/qa-stock-status-results.json`, `_verify/qa-closing-results.json` and
# `_verify/qa-order-management.results.json` are named as "Raw output" by the m2 reports
# and are tracked evidence.
#
# WATCH OUT — those three are also what the frozen `_verify/qa-*.py` runners overwrite
# UNCONDITIONALLY on every run (e.g. `_verify/qa-stock-status.py` writes its results file
# with no flag and no guard). Running an m2-round runner in-tree therefore destroys the
# snapshot its own report cites; it happened on 2026-08-09 and was reverted. Run those
# from a copy of the repo, never in place.
qa-*-prehandoff-results.json
qa-*-results.tmp.json

# Scratch probes. Verification passes write throwaway scripts at the repo root; they are
# never part of the spec set and must not reach a public commit.
/_*.py
/scratch/
